<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish Permanent pays 12.6 mln stg for CHL.</title>
<headline>Irish Permanent pays 12.6 mln stg for CHL.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish Permanent Plc paid 12.6 million sterling for UK mortgage house Capital Home Loans (CHL), a spokesperson said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Irish Permanent paid approximately 10.1 million sterling for the net assets of the company.</p>
<p>It paid a premium of 1.25 percent or 2.5 million in respect of a mortgage portfolio of 200 million sterling giving a total consideration of 12.6 million sterling.</p>
<p>CHL Ltd is a wholly-owned unit of Credit Foncier de France.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9775</p>
